WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.493
The program carries one rule forward
unchanged: misconfigurations rated Critical

2
00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:10.625
or High are remediated and verified
before any certificate workload migrates.

3
00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:14.730
Migrating from a CA that can be
made to issue arbitrary credentials

4
00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.762
propagates the weakness into
whatever trusts the hierarchy next.

5
00:00:18.762 --> 00:00:23.030
And under the bring-your-own-CA
model the program recommends,

6
00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:27.725
the new Cloud PKI issuing CA chains
to the existing AD CS hierarchy,

7
00:00:27.725 --> 00:00:31.225
so it inherits every weakness
the day it goes live.

8
00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:36.400
The ESC names come from SpecterOps' 2021
research; Microsoft adopted the same

9
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:41.413
labels in Defender for Identity, which
is why they're the shared vocabulary.

10
00:00:41.413 --> 00:00:44.713
The book uses them only as
labels for defensive checks.

11
00:00:44.713 --> 00:00:47.400
The classes live in four control points.

12
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.112
Template objects hold ESC1 through ESC4.

13
00:00:51.112 --> 00:00:57.320
The Public Key Services objects hold
ESC5, which Defender for Identity doesn't

14
00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:03.624
assess, so detection is an ACL review plus
directory change auditing, event 5136.

15
00:01:03.624 --> 00:01:08.026
The CA's own configuration
holds ESC6 and ESC7,

16
00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:11.963
and HTTP enrollment endpoints hold ESC8.

17
00:01:11.963 --> 00:01:17.194
Certificate template assessments are
available to every customer with AD CS;

18
00:01:17.194 --> 00:01:21.861
CA assessments need a Defender for
Identity sensor on the AD CS server,

19
00:01:21.861 --> 00:01:25.000
so install it on every
enterprise CA that stays.

20
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.700
Two caveats from the book.

21
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:32.346
In GCC, Defender for Identity uses the
security dot microsoft dot com portal;

22
00:01:32.346 --> 00:01:37.813
Microsoft says new features reach GCC,
GCC High and DoD within ninety days

23
00:01:37.813 --> 00:01:43.100
of commercial release, but preview
features may not be supported there.

24
00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.877
The ESC1 and ESC6 assessments
are still labeled preview,

25
00:01:46.877 --> 00:01:52.150
so confirm they appear in your tenant,
and run the manual checks in the meantime.
